---
config:
  flowchart:
    nodeSpacing: 24
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: How a run starts and what it reaches
    accDescr: An administrator configures the app and starts a dry run on the settings page, whose controllers start the synchronization, or a run, which the controllers queue as a background job. Nextcloud's cron starts the scheduled background job and the queued one, which start the synchronization as well. On the server, the administrator starts runs with the occ commands. The synchronization builds the path of every document with the path templates, reads Paperless-ngx through the Paperless client, which calls its REST API with the token, and writes the files of the target user through the storage. Everything but the administrator and Paperless-ngx runs inside the Nextcloud server.

    admin(["Administrator"])
    subgraph nextcloud ["Nextcloud server"]
        settings["Settings page<br>and controllers"]
        commands["occ<br>commands"]
        cron(["Nextcloud cron"])
        job["`Background jobs<br>*scheduled, and<br>Synchronize now*`"]
        sync["Synchronization"]
        template["Path<br>templates"]
        storage["Storage"]
        client["Paperless<br>client"]
        files[("Files of the<br>target user")]
    end
    paperless[("Paperless-ngx")]

    admin -- "configure,<br>dry run, run" ---> settings
    admin -- "run, status,<br>forget" ---> commands
    cron --> job
    settings -- "dry run" --> sync
    settings -- "queue a run" --> job
    commands --> sync
    job --> sync
    sync --> template & storage & client
    storage --> files
    client -- "REST API<br>with the token" --> paperless
    %% An invisible link draws Paperless-ngx below the Nextcloud server, not beside it.
    files ~~~ paperless

    classDef paperless fill:#17803d2e,stroke:#17803d,stroke-width:2px
    classDef nextcloud fill:#0082c92e,stroke:#0082c9,stroke-width:2px
    class paperless paperless
    class files nextcloud
